message: "If you use quadsim in your research, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "quadsim: a drone reinforcement-learning and imitation-learning research framework on Isaac Lab"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Tuan
    alias: TuanDinh97
repository-code: "https://github.com/TuanDinh97/Drone_Sim_RL"
license: BSD-3-Clause
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-11-02"
keywords:
  - reinforcement learning
  - imitation learning
  - vision-language-action
  - quadrotor
  - drone
  - Isaac Lab
  - sim-to-real
  - benchmark
abstract: >-
  quadsim is a modular, configuration-driven framework for drone reinforcement learning and imitation learning on
  NVIDIA Isaac Lab: validated multirotor physics and sensor models, interchangeable control interfaces from motor
  commands to position set-points, configurable observation / reward / constraint / curriculum terms, PPO, SAC, TD3
  and PPO-Lagrangian, racing, multi-agent and language-conditioned tasks, demonstration recording with LeRobot export,
  closed-loop evaluation of local or remote (openpi-protocol) vision-language-action policies, benchmark suites with
  in- and out-of-distribution conditions, and a PX4 SITL deployment pipeline.
